### Performance Results

Measurement: 15 runs, skip first 5 warmup, mean of 10. All 113 JOB queries.

| Config | none-split (s) | node-based (s) | Gap (s) | Gap (%) |
|--------|---------------:|---------------:|--------:|--------:|
| All passes ON (baseline, pre-Opt-10) | 9.682 | 10.716 | +1.035 | +10.7% |
| JFP disabled (reference) | 15.732 | 14.416 | -1.316 | -8.4% |
| **Opt-10 (Gap 1 done)** | **9.597** | **10.565** | **+0.968** | **+10.1%** |

#### Impact Analysis

| Metric | Value |
|--------|------:|
| Node-based improvement | -0.151s (10.716 -> 10.565) |
| None-split change | -0.085s (9.682 -> 9.597, measurement noise) |
| **Gap reduction** | **0.067s** (1.035 -> 0.968) |
| **% of original gap closed** | **6.5%** |
| JFP asymmetry reduction | 2.350s -> 2.283s (-0.067s) |

#### Assessment

Gap 1 fix had **modest impact** (6.5% of gap closed), consistent with the pre-
implementation prediction that "expected impact is modest on its own." The none-
split variation (-0.085s) is measurement noise (spread across many queries, max
per-query diff ~10ms).

The Gap 1 fix is a necessary enabler but most of the JFP asymmetry comes from
**Gap 2: cross-boundary filter loss**. Within a single subquery, temp tables are
often probe-side with large build sides, so bloom filters rarely trigger
(`CanUseBloomFilter()` requires probe > build cardinality). The range filters
pushed to temp tables are typically too broad to meaningfully filter.

#### Revised Gap Impact Estimates (post-measurement)

| Gap | Pre-estimate | Measured | Notes |
|-----|-------------|----------|-------|
| Gap 1: temp as target | ~25-35% | **~6.5%** | Range filters too broad; bloom rarely triggers |
| Gap 2: cross-boundary | ~60-70% | **~88-90%** (revised) | Dominant: filters from other subqueries can't reach |
| Gap 3: no zone maps | ~5% | ~5% | Unchanged, inherent |

Gap 1 and Gap 2 overlap less than initially estimated. Most of the "temp as target"
scenario involves filters that are too broad to help, while the real impact is
the cross-boundary loss of selective bloom filters.

