## Opt-12: Failed Experiment — TempCollectionStatistics + Transitive BF (REVERTED/PENDING)

### What was attempted

Three changes bundled as Opt-12:

**Opt-12a**: Register `TempCollectionStatistics` on the `scan_temp_collection` table
function so DuckDB's optimizer gets per-column min/max for temp tables. The function
`TempCollectionStatistics()` already existed in `duckdb_adapter.cpp` but was never
wired up to the table function's `statistics_extended` callback.

**Opt-12b**: Transitive bloom filter injection. When `temp.A = X.B` and `X.B = Y.C`
in the SQL, the BF from temp can also filter Y.C even though there is no direct
temp→Y join. Added `find_all_join_partners` lambda to `ApplyCrossSubPlanOptimizations`
that scans the SQL for all equality partners of a column, then tries each as a BF
target (subject to the existing match_rate < 0.25 guard).

**Opt-12c**: Raised `kBFMaxTempCard` from 100000 to 2000000. (Later folded into Opt-11.)

### Files changed (AQP Middleware, branch topdown_fix)

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp` (line 214) | Added `func.statistics_extended = TempCollectionStatistics` (Opt-12a) |
| `src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp` (line 1788) | Added `IsNumeric()` guard on stats creation to prevent StringStats bug |
| `src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp` (line 1802) | Added `!col_stats[ci]` null guard in per-chunk scan loop |
| `src/split/ir_query_splitter.cpp` (~line 2970) | Added `find_all_join_partners` lambda for transitive BF targets (Opt-12b) |
| `src/split/ir_query_splitter.cpp` (line 2964) | Raised `kBFMaxTempCard` to 2000000 (Opt-12c, later folded into Opt-11) |

### Correctness Bug Found (Opt-12a)

`BaseStatistics::CreateEmpty()` for VARCHAR columns initializes `StringStats` with
`max_string_length=0` and inverted min/max (`min=0xFF*`, `max=0x00*`). The stats
computation code was calling `CreateEmpty()` for ALL column types but only updating
numeric stats — VARCHAR columns kept the "empty" defaults. When the optimizer saw
`max_string_length=0` it concluded no valid strings exist and pruned joins
incorrectly. Query 17f returned `=|` instead of `'El Galgo PornoStar', Blanquito|`.

**Fix**: Only create stats for `types[ci].IsNumeric()`, leaving non-numeric columns
as `nullptr` (no stats). This fixed the correctness bug but the performance
regression remained.

### Performance Results (Opt-12a+12b+12c combined)

