## Opt-14: Selectivity Check for Middleware BFs (REVERTED)

### What

DuckDB wraps native JFP bloom filters in `SelectivityOptionalFilter` (threshold
0.25, check 75 vectors) that auto-disables ineffective filters. Middleware BFs at
`physical_table_scan.cpp:209-264` were always-on. Added a simple selectivity
counter to `AQPBloomScanFilter`: after N chunks, if accepted/total > threshold,
disable the BF for the rest of the scan.

### Files Changed (DuckDB, branch AQP_JIT_152)

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `src/include/duckdb/execution/aqp_jit.hpp` | Added `sel_vectors_seen`, `sel_tuples_accepted`, `sel_tuples_total`, `sel_disabled` fields + `UpdateSelectivity()` method to `AQPBloomScanFilter` |
| `src/execution/operator/scan/physical_table_scan.cpp` | Skip disabled BFs, call `UpdateSelectivity()` after each BF application |

### Expected Impact

10-25ms improvement by disabling ineffective BFs on large temp tables (prevents
scan overhead on BFs with >25% selectivity).

### Correctness

All 113 JOB queries pass correctness verification.

