## Opt-3 Removal: Column Stats Infrastructure Cleanup (DONE)

### What

Opt-3 (originally added in commit `9228d79`, DuckDB commit `d251231`) injected
per-column min/max statistics into `LogicalColumnDataGet::column_stats` so that
DuckDB's statistics propagator (`propagate_get.cpp`) could use them during join
ordering. This was effective on DuckDB 1.3.2 but **had zero measurable effect on
DuckDB 1.5.2** — A/B testing the 10 heaviest queries (8 runs each, 3 warmup)
showed deltas of -8.4ms to +8.0ms, all within noise.

The stats infrastructure involved two paths:
- **Path A (Opt-3, active)**: StoredTempResult::column_stats → node_based_splitter
  → MergeDataChunk → LogicalColumnDataGet::column_stats → propagate_get.cpp
- **Path B (Opt-12a, disabled)**: StoredTempResult::column_stats →
  TempCollectionBind → TempCollectionStatistics callback (caused +0.416s regression)

Both paths shared the same eager per-column min/max scan in
`ExecuteSQLandCreateTempTable` and `ExecuteSpeculativeAndCreateTempTable`, which
scanned the entire ColumnDataCollection to compute column statistics. This scan
was the dominant cost captured by `extra_materialization` in the MW breakdown.

### Why No Effect on 1.5.2

DuckDB 1.5.2's optimizer relies on bloom filters and adaptive
`SelectivityOptionalFilter` for join-time filtering. These mechanisms are
pipeline-internal and ignore per-column min/max from LogicalColumnDataGet. The
column stats only affected the cost model for join ordering, but the cardinality
estimate alone (already provided via `EstimateCardinality`) gives the optimizer
sufficient information.

### Files Changed

#### AQP Middleware (branch topdown_fix)

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `include/adapters/duckdb_adapter.h` | Removed `column_stats` field from `StoredTempResult`, removed `TempCollectionStatistics` declaration |
| `src/adapters/duckdb_adapter.cpp` | Removed `column_stats` from `TempCollectionFunctionData`, removed `TempCollectionStatistics` function definition, removed eager stats scan from `ExecuteSQLandCreateTempTable` and `ExecuteSpeculativeAndCreateTempTable`, removed `column_stats` copying in `TempCollectionBind` |
| `src/split/node_based_splitter.cpp` | Removed col_stats_copy construction and `column_stats` parameter from `MergeDataChunk` call |

#### DuckDB (branch AQP_JIT_152)

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `src/include/duckdb/planner/operator/logical_column_data_get.hpp` | Removed `column_stats` field |
| `src/optimizer/statistics/operator/propagate_get.cpp` | Removed 9-line Opt-3 stats injection block from `PropagateStatistics(LogicalColumnDataGet&)` |
| `src/include/duckdb/optimizer/query_split/subquery_preparer.hpp` | Removed `column_stats` parameter from `MergeDataChunk` declaration |
| `src/optimizer/query_split/subquery_preparer.cpp` | Removed `column_stats` parameter from `MergeDataChunk` definition |

### Correctness

All 113 JOB queries pass correctness verification. Both AQP_middleware and DuckDB
build successfully.

